# ==============================================================================
# Trace — .gitattributes
#
# Two jobs:
#   1. Route every binary type an Unreal project accumulates through Git LFS.
#   2. Force deterministic LF line endings on all text, so a Windows and a macOS
#      developer never produce a whole-file diff by opening the same file.
#
# LFS setup for a fresh clone:      ./Scripts/setup-lfs.sh
#
# Patterns are case-sensitive on case-sensitive filesystems (Linux CI, APFS
# volumes formatted case-sensitive). Uppercase duplicates are listed for the
# extensions that DCC tools most often emit in caps (.PNG from some exporters,
# .TGA / .FBX from older Max/Maya pipelines).
#
# THIS REPO HAS REAL ASSETS. As of 2026-08-09: 641 files / 5.14 MiB in LFS (the
# baked arena's 572 external actors, 66 materials, 3 levels). Earlier docs called
# the project "asset-free"; that has not been true since the arena was baked, and
# the locking rules below are load-bearing rather than theoretical.
#
# `lockable` is set on the merge-hostile Unreal formats (.uasset/.umap/.fbx).
# Those files cannot be merged — two people editing one is always data loss —
# so the workflow is:
#     git pull
#     Scripts/lock.sh   Content/Maps/Arena_Baked.umap   # or: git lfs lock <path>
#     ... edit, commit, push ...
#     Scripts/unlock.sh Content/Maps/Arena_Baked.umap   # or: git lfs unlock <path>
# `git lfs locks` lists who holds what. Locked files are checked out read-only
# (-r--r--r--) for everyone else, which is the point: the OS stops you before Git
# has to. Do not chmod it away — take the lock. Full workflow: docs/GITHUB.md §4.
#
# ONE FILE PER ACTOR CHANGES WHAT YOU LOCK, NOT WHETHER YOU LOCK (spec v15 §1.6).
# /Game/Maps/Arena_Baked has "Use External Actors" on, so the arena is not one
# .umap — it is a ~6 KB .umap plus one .uasset per actor under
#     Content/__ExternalActors__/Maps/Arena_Baked/<2 hex>/<2 hex>/<guid>.uasset
# Those are .uasset, so the rule above already covers them: LFS, and lockable.
# That combination is the entire payoff of the migration. Before it, moving one
# wall meant locking the whole level and everybody else waited; now two people
# lock two actors and neither notices the other. The unreadable GUID filenames
# are the engine's, not ours — find the actor by its LABEL in the World Outliner
# (Wall_North_01, Cover_37, Goal_Ring_Rim_12; the numbering is zero-padded to two
# digits, so Cover_37 and NOT Cover_037) and either let the editor's source
# control integration lock the file behind it, or run `Scripts/lock.sh Cover_37`,
# which resolves the label to its package for you.
#
# Produce or re-produce that map with:  Scripts/bake-arena.sh --force
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: let Git decide, but normalise anything it detects as text to LF in
# the repository. Explicit rules below override this.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto eol=lf

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unreal binary asset formats — LFS + lockable
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.uasset  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text lockable
*.umap    filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text lockable
*.UASSET  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text lockable
*.UMAP    filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text lockable
*.ubulk   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.uexp    filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.uptnl   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.udk     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.upk     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3D / DCC source files — LFS, and lockable for the ones artists co-edit
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.fbx     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text lockable
*.FBX     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text lockable
*.obj     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.3ds     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.abc     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.blend   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text lockable
*.ma      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text lockable
*.mb      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text lockable
*.max     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text lockable
*.dae     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.glb     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.gltf    filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
